{"term":"wipe","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:7eed0bf8745babe4fe","definition":"To move an object over, maintaining contact, with the intention of removing some substance from the surface. (Compare rub.)","example":"Melissa wiped her glasses with her shirt.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wipe#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:6100f7d2cd1267dffe","definition":"To smear (a substance) with this kind of motion.","example":"You've wiped grease all over your shirt.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wipe#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ee7e49765a5bb8241f","definition":"To remove by rubbing; to rub off; to obliterate; usually followed by away, off, or out.","example":"Some natural tears they dropped, but wiped them soon.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"transitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wipe#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:45c73d8c370ae92133","definition":"To clean (the anus, buttocks and/or genitals) after defecation or urination.","example":"I had nothing to wipe my bum with.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"ambitransitive","register":"ambitransitive","wordFamily":[],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wipe#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:65cfea15ae98657c1c","definition":"To eras